term follow-up</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Clinical Oncology</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>21</volume><issue>13</issue><fpage>2583</fpage><lpage>2588</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12829679</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bousquet</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Confavreux</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Magn&#x000e9;</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Outcome and prognostic factors in breast sarcoma: a multicenter study from the rare cancer network</article-title><source><italic>Radiotherapy and Oncology</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>85</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>355</fpage><lpage>361</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18023492</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Buinauskas</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>ER</given-names></name><name><surname>Cole</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Antigenic behavior of Walker 256 tumor in Sprague-Dawley rats</article-title><source><italic>Surgery</italic></source><year>1966</year><volume>60</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>902</fpage><lpage>907</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5921635</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Papac</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Spontaneous regression of cancer: possible mechanisms</article-title><source><italic>In Vivo</italic></source><year>1998</year><volume>12</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>571</fpage><lpage>578</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9891219</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sim</surname><given-names>BKL</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Reilly</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Liang</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A recombinant human angiostatin protein inhibits experimental primary and metastatic cancer</article-title><source><italic>Cancer Research</italic></source><year>1997</year><volume>57</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>1329</fpage><lpage>1334</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9102221</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holmgren</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Reilly</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Folkman</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dormancy of micrometastases: balanced proliferation and apoptosis in the presence of angiogenesis suppression</article-title><source><italic>Nature Medicine</italic></source><year>1995</year><volume>1</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>149</fpage><lpage>153</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7585012</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cole</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Efforts to explain spontaneous regression of cancer</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Surgical Oncology</italic></source><year>1981</year><volume>17</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>201</fpage><lpage>209</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6166811</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McCann</surname><given-names>FV</given-names></name><name><surname>Pettengill</surname><given-names>OS</given-names></name><name><surname>Cole</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Russell</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Sorenson</surname><given-names>GD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Calcium spike electrogenesis and other electrical activity in continuously cultured small cell carcinoma of the lung</article-title><source><italic>Science</italic></source><year>1981</year><volume>212</volume><issue>4499</issue><fpage>1155</fpage><lpage>1157</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6262914</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hoption Cann</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>van Netten</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>van Netten</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Glover</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Spontaneous regression: a hidden treasure buried in time</article-title><source><italic>Medical Hypotheses</italic></source><year>2002</year><volume>58</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>119</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11812185</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kappauf</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Gallmeier</surname><given-names>WM</given-names></name><name><surname>W&#x000fc;nsch</surname><given-names>PH</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Complete spontaneous remission in a patient with metastatic non-small-cell lung cancer. Case report, review of literature, and discussion of possible biological pathways involved</article-title><source><italic>Annals of Oncology</italic></source><year>1997</year><volume>8</volume><issue>10</issue><fpage>1031</fpage><lpage>1039</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9402178</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Esteller</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Epigenetics in cancer</article-title><source><italic>The New England Journal of Medicine</italic></source><year>2008</year><volume>358</volume><issue>11</issue><fpage>1148</fpage><lpage>1159</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18337604</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sugimura</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ushijima</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genetic and epigenetic alterations in carcinogenesis</article-title><source><italic>Mutation Research/Reviews in Mutation Research</italic></source><year>2000</year><volume>462</volume><issue>2-3</issue><fpage>235</fpage><lpage>246</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Xiang</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Moyana</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Regression of engineered myeloma cells secreting interferon-<italic>&#x003b3;</italic>-inducing factor is mediated by both CD4<sup>+</sup>/CD8<sup>+</sup> T and natural killer cells</article-title><source><italic>Leukemia Research</italic></source><year>2001</year><volume>25</volume><issue>10</issue><fpage>909</fpage><lpage>915</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11532525</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sabat&#x000e9;</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Llauger</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Torrubia</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Amores</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Franquet</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Osteosarcoma of the abdominal wall with spontaneous regression of lung metastases</article-title><source><italic>American Journal of Roentgenology</italic></source><year>1998</year><volume>171</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>691</fpage><lpage>692</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9725297</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ota</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Shinagawa</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ueoka</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Spontaneous regression of metastatic endometrial stromal sarcoma</article-title><source><italic>Japanese Journal of Clinical Oncology</italic></source><year>2002</year><volume>32</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>71</fpage><lpage>74</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11948233</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="fig1" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>An ulcerated bruise-like lesion in the left breast, consistent with the typical appearanceof a breast angiosarcoma.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="SRCM2008-940656.001"/></fig><fig id="fig2" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Chest radiograph showing multiple lung metastases.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="SRCM2008-940656.002"/></fig><fig id="fig3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Repeat chest radiograph performed three months later showing a significant reduction insize and number of lung metastases.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="SRCM2008-940656.003"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>